Brightness: the slider's bottom is dim, not black (spesblmin, default 48 of 0x7ff).

all35: the slider went down to 1 (Control Center), and every wake after restored "brightness 1":
1..255 mapped straight onto the panel's 1..0x7ff put 1 at level 8, black on this OLED, so the phone
seemed not to wake. 1..255 now map onto spesblmin..0x7ff; 0 (the end of the lock fade) stays 1.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -500,14 +500,32 @@
 	return true;
 }
 
-/* fWL gate held. 0..255 -> the panel's 1..0x7ff, kept as the level the lock fade starts from. */
+/*
+ * fWL gate held. 0 -> the panel's 1 (the end of the lock fade); 1..255 -> spesblmin..0x7ff, kept as
+ * the level the lock fade starts from. Straight 1..0x7ff put the slider's bottom at level 8, black
+ * on this OLED: all35 woke "black" after the slider had gone to 1 (an iPhone's lowest is dim, not off).
+ */
+static uint32_t
+sweet_bl_floor(void)
+{
+	static uint32_t floor;
+	if (floor == 0) {
+		uint32_t v = 48;
+		(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("spesblmin", &v, sizeof(v));
+		floor = v < 1 ? 1 : (v > 0x400 ? 0x400 : v);
+	}
+	return floor;
+}
